TODO(project): two workflows, and exactly two status check names.

  verify         the project typecheck, lint and test commands, plus `node scripts/check-docs.mjs`
                 and `node --test .claude/hooks/tests/*.test.mjs scripts/tests/*.test.mjs`
  allowed-paths  `node scripts/check-allowed-paths.mjs`, and nothing else

Do not split into six jobs. Branch protection points at those two names, and every additional job
name is another thing that must be configured, kept green, and explained.

Do not enable branch protection until `verify` has passed at least once. A required check that has
never passed blocks every pull request, including the operator's, and the only way out is to disable
the protection you just configured.
